::id(cli.board)

`sisho-board`: interactive operating dashboard and board for the Tomet ecosystem.

Status: decided 2026-10-20, extracted into standalone repository `sisho-board` with `sisho-board-sdk`.

=[ Overview ]

`sisho-board` provides a dedicated operating dashboard for a Tomet vault or repository: inspecting core tool versions, measuring vault readiness and health (`%`), managing extension execution trust, viewing extension board panes, viewing broken links, and running checks or fixes on demand.

It runs standalone as `sisho-board [path]`, or through `sisho` as `sisho board [path]`. For non-interactive inspection or CI reporting, `sisho-board --report [path]` (`-r`) prints a formatted readiness report and `sisho-board --json [path]` prints the structured `HealthReport` JSON.

=[ Two-tier Design: Board & Counter ]

1. **Board (Information Display)**:
   - **Tools & Extensions (Built-in Standard Card)**: Displays versions and compatibility status of core tools (`tomet`, `twrit`, `catasto`), along with installed `sisho-<word>` extensions discovered on `PATH` and their trust status (`Untrusted`, `Allowed`, `Denied`).
   - **Integrity & Checks (Built-in Standard Card)**: Displays status, exit code, and duration of each step in `check`, with an output preview pane showing stdout/stderr of the selected step.
   - **Vault Readiness & Health (Built-in Standard Card)**: Displays an overall readiness percentage gauge bar (`[█████████░]  92% Overall Readiness`) and six selectable readiness pillars whose actionable file lists and diagnostics appear in the preview pane when selected:
     1. **Tomet Coverage (`tomet_coverage`)**: `.tmt` source documents and generated `.md` artifacts (`CLAUDE.md`, `Generated from ` header, or `::export(path: ...)` targets) vs unmigrated hand-written `.md` files.
     2. **`::id` Declaration (`id_coverage`)**: share of author-owned `.tmt` documents declaring `::id(...)`.
     3. **`::kind` & Blueprint (`kind_coverage`)**: share of author-owned `.tmt` documents declaring `::kind(...)` or `::blueprint(...)`, enriched with `tomet stats --json` corpus breakdowns.
     4. **Link Health (`link_health`)**: unbroken links vs total checked links from `tomet check-links --json`.
     5. **Writ & Catasto Governance (`governance`)**: presence of `.writ.tmt`, guarded `@rule(...)` blocks, and `catasto.lock` consistency.
     6. **Cleanliness & Freshness (`cleanliness`)**: absence of `@draft` markers and validation warnings/errors, plus documentation vs code modification freshness.
   - **Extension Board Panes (External Extensions)**: Displays custom panes (`BoardPane`) emitted by allowed extensions via `sisho-<word> --sisho-board-pane <path>`, including a percentage `BoardGauge` bar and selectable `BoardItem` rows whose details appear in the preview pane. Extensions can appear either in the aggregate `Extension Panes` card (filtered by `hidden_extension_panes`) or as dedicated standalone panes (`PaneId::Extension(word)`) placed directly into a `BoardView`.
   - **Broken Links (Built-in Standard Card)**: Displays summary and entries of broken links found by `tomet check-links --json`.

2. **Counter (Execution Selection)**:
   - Unified two-level navigation + view tabs:
     - `Tab` / `BackTab` / `1`..`9` (or `[` / `]`): Switch between configured `BoardView` tabs displayed in the `HeaderBar` (also resets active-pane mode and snaps pane focus to a visible pane if needed).
     - **Pane Selection Mode (`!pane_active`)**:
       - `←` `↑` `↓` `→`: Move 2D spatial focus across panes in the active `BoardView` (`↑`/`↓` within the current column, `←`/`→` proportionally across columns).
       - `Enter`: Activate/enter the selected pane (`[ACTIVE]`) to explore its items.
       - `Esc` / `q`: Exit the board.
     - **Active Pane Mode (`pane_active`)**:
       - `↑` / `k`, `↓` / `j`: Navigate items or scroll within the active pane (`PageUp` / `PageDown` / `Home` scroll preview).
       - `Esc`: Exit active pane mode back to 2D pane selection (`q` exits the board).
       - `a` / `Enter` (when focused on `Tools & Extensions`): Open the trust confirmation prompt (`[y] Allow / [d] Deny / [u] Untrusted / [n/Esc] Cancel`) for the selected extension. On confirmation, `sisho-board` delegates the update to `sisho --allow`, `sisho --deny`, or `sisho --untrust` using the extension's canonical path.
       - `Enter` / `e` (when focused on `Broken Links`): Open the selected link's source file in an editor at the broken line, restoring the board and re-verifying links on return.
       - `Enter` / `e` (when focused on `Integrity & Checks`, `Vault Readiness & Health`, `Extension Panes`, or a standalone extension pane): Jump focus to `Output Preview` when present in the active view.
     - **Global Board Actions** (available in both Pane Selection and Active Pane modes):
       - `v`: Open the **Board Layout Editor** modal using a **Grab & Drop** model (with immediate persistence to `board.json`):
       - Displays a top bar (`View X/Y`, visual `Left % | Right %` split bar, and `[MOVING]` / rename / confirmation prompts) above three columns (`Left Column`, `Right Column`, and `Available`).
       - `↑` / `k`, `↓` / `j`, `←` / `h` / `BackTab`, `→` / `l` / `Tab`: Move the cursor across panes and columns when not grabbed.
       - `Space` / `Enter`: Grab the selected pane (`» ... [MOVING]`) or drop it; when pressed in `Available`, adds the pane to `Left` and immediately grabs it for positioning.
       - While grabbed: `↑`/`k` and `↓`/`j` move the pane up/down within its column; `←`/`h` moves from `Right` to `Left`; `→`/`l` moves from `Left` to `Right`, or from `Right` hides to `Available` and drops it; `Esc` releases the grab without closing the modal.
       - `Delete` / `Backspace` (in `Left`/`Right` when not grabbed): Remove/hide the selected pane to `Available`.
       - `+` / `=` and `-` / `_`: Adjust the selected pane's vertical weight (`5..=100`, step `5`); `<` / `>`: adjust `left_ratio` (`20..=80`, step `5`).
       - `[` / `]`: Switch views; `n`: add a new view; `R`: rename active view inline (`Enter` save, `Esc` cancel); `D`: delete active view (with confirmation; blocked if only 1 view remains); `r`: reset views to default (with confirmation); `u`: undo up to 20 edits; `Esc` (when not grabbed) / `v`: close the editor.
     - `c`: Execute check steps, re-evaluate Vault Readiness & Health, and refresh allowed extension board panes.
     - `f`: Execute fix steps. Always prompts for confirmation (`Apply fixes? [y/N]`) before any file write occurs, and refreshes Vault Readiness & Health upon completion.
     - `l`: Re-run the link check (`tomet check-links --json`).
     - `x`: Open the global TUI extension launcher modal from any pane. Lists active extensions excluding `board` and `Denied`: `Allowed` extensions whose `--sisho-extension-info` declares `capabilities.tui = true`, plus `Untrusted` active extensions (so users can inspect or allow them without leaving the launcher). Each entry shows extension `word`, `about` (when queried), `trust`, and `path`. Inside the launcher: `↑` / `k`, `↓` / `j` navigate; `Enter` launches an `Allowed` TUI extension with terminal handover (`current_dir` set to the board directory and no positional arguments) or opens the trust confirmation prompt if `Untrusted`; `a` opens the trust confirmation prompt; `Esc` / `x` closes the launcher.
     - `q`: Exit the board.

=[ Non-interactive CLI Modes (`--report` and `--json`) ]

- `sisho-board --report [path]` (`-r`): Evaluates the six readiness pillars and link health for `path` (default `.`) without opening the TUI, prints a human-readable summary with the `%` gauge bar and actionable findings for any non-100% pillars, and exits 0.
- `sisho-board --json [path]`: Evaluates the six readiness pillars and link health for `path` without opening the TUI, prints the `HealthReport` JSON object to standard output, and exits 0.

=[ Extension Trust (`~/.local/share/sisho/trust.json` via `sisho`) ]

- **Trust Ownership**: `sisho` is the sole owner of `~/.local/share/sisho/trust.json` (`$XDG_DATA_HOME/sisho/trust.json`). `sisho-board` never reads or writes `trust.json` directly; instead it queries `sisho --list --json` on startup and delegates trust changes via `sisho --allow <path>`, `sisho --deny <path>`, or `sisho --untrust <path>` after explicit user confirmation (`[y] Allow / [d] Deny / [u] Untrusted / [n/Esc] Cancel`).
- **Default Untrusted Policy**: If `sisho` is missing or older, `sisho-board` falls back to scanning `PATH` without executing any binary and treats every extension as `Untrusted`. `sisho-board` never executes an `Untrusted` or `Denied` extension for `--sisho-extension-info`, `--sisho-board-pane`, editor fallback, or launcher handover.
- **Per-Extension Environments**: When querying or launching an `Allowed` extension, `sisho-board` sets `SISHO_CONFIG_DIR` (`$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sisho/<word>` or `$HOME/.config/sisho/<word>`) and `SISHO_DATA_DIR` (`$XDG_DATA_HOME/sisho/<word>` or `$HOME/.local/share/sisho/<word>`).

=[ Board UI Configuration (`~/.config/sisho/board/board.json`) ]

- **Config Location**: `$SISHO_CONFIG_DIR/board.json` if `SISHO_CONFIG_DIR` is set and non-empty; otherwise `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/sisho/board/board.json` if `XDG_CONFIG_HOME` is set and non-empty; otherwise `$HOME/.config/sisho/board/board.json` (matching `sisho_sdk::config_dir("board")`).
- **Portable UI State (`schema_version: 2`)**: `board.json` stores only portable UI layout preferences, with zero binary paths and zero trust state:
  - `schema_version`: Currently `2`.
  - `views`: Ordered list of named `BoardView` presets (`name`, `left_ratio` clamped to `20..=80` defaulting to `45`, `left` and `right` lists of `PaneSlot { pane: PaneId, weight: u16 }` with `weight` normalized to `1..=100`). Defaults to a single `"Overview"` view (`left_ratio: 45`, `left: [Extensions (w:55), BrokenLinks (w:45)]`, `right: [Health (w:25), Checks (w:25), ExtensionPanes (w:20), OutputPreview (w:30)]`). If `views` is empty on load, it falls back to the default view; duplicate panes within a view are deduplicated.
  - `active_view`: 0-based index of the active `BoardView`, clamped to `0..views.len()`.
  - `hidden_extension_panes`: Extension words filtered out of the aggregate `ExtensionPanes` pane without affecting trust.
- **Pane Identifiers (`PaneId`)**: Built-in variants (`checks`, `health`, `extensions`, `broken_links`, `extension_panes`, `output_preview`) and standalone extension panes (`extension("<word>")`) backed by an allowed extension's `--sisho-board-pane` output. When only one column in a `BoardView` contains panes, it expands to 100% width; when both columns are empty, the board displays a hint to press `v` to customize the layout.

=[ Board Pane Protocol (`--sisho-board-pane`) ]

An extension that is marked `Allowed` is queried with `sisho-<word> --sisho-board-pane <path>`. If it supports board panes, it outputs a single `BoardPane` JSON object (defined in `sisho-board-sdk`) and exits 0:
- `schema_version`: `1`
- `title`: Pane title string
- `gauge`: Optional `{ "label": "...", "percent": 0..=100 }`
- `items`: List of `{ "label": "...", "value": "...", "status": "pass|warn|fail|info", "detail": "..." }`
- `summary`: Optional fallback summary text for the preview pane

=[ Crate Architecture ]

The `sisho-board` workspace is structured into four dependency layers enforced by `.writ.tmt`:
- **Layer 0**: `sisho-board-config` (portable `board.json` configuration, `BoardView`, and `PaneId` schema), `sisho-board-sdk` (Board Pane JSON schema), and `sisho-board-run` (jobserver-gated `Step` subprocess runner, sole owner of `std::process` in `crates/*`).
- **Layer 1**: `sisho-board-health` (six-pillar `Vault Readiness & Health` engine and `tomet check-links` report parser) and `sisho-board-core` (state `Model`, `sisho` trust delegation, extension discovery, editor resolution, and `board.json` config).
- **Layer 2**: `sisho-board-tui` (Ratatui rendering, terminal `Screen` guard, and interactive event loop; sole owner of `ratatui` and `crossterm` in `crates/*`).
- **Layer 3**: `app` (`sisho-board` CLI binary).
